            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for dance, then the Marathi for a stage."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: आगगाडी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आगगाडी — āggāḍī — \"a train; a steam train\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आगगाडी पुलावरून हळू जाते. āggāḍī pulāvarūn haḷū jāte. The train goes slowly over the bridge."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. Plural: आगगाड्या, āggāḍyā."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The plural is आगगाड्या; in everyday talk गाडी alone often means the train."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आगगाडी (āggāḍī) is a Marathi compound from the age of steam: आग, \"fire\", inherited from Sanskrit agni (CDIAL 55), and गाडी, \"a cart\", inherited from gāḍḍa (CDIAL 4116)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
